*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated fixtures are compared byte-for-byte against a regenerated copy, so
# their line endings must not depend on the checkout platform.
#
# `bench/fixtures/generate-eval-vault.mjs` writes LF. With `core.autocrlf=true`
# — the Windows default — checkout rewrites these files to CRLF, so a
# regeneration immediately reports 55 modified files in `git status` and the
# tree can never be clean. `git diff` hides it, because diff normalizes both
# sides before comparing and reports no change; that is what makes this worth
# pinning rather than documenting, since the obvious check passes while the
# tree is dirty. Holding them at LF everywhere makes regenerate-and-compare
# mean the same thing on every platform.
bench/fixtures/eval-vault/** text eol=lf
bench/datasets/*.json text eol=lf
